IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia71-types`
IMPORT `ia71-status`
IMPORT `ia71-offences`

-- Immigration Act 1971 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Immigration case` HAS
    `the person`                                        IS A `Person facts`
    `a leave extension`                                 IS A MAYBE `Leave extension facts`
    `the day in question`                               IS A DATE
    `an offence`                                        IS A MAYBE `Offence facts`

DECLARE `Immigration position` HAS
    `right of abode`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `requires leave to enter`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `leave extended by s 3C on the day`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `maximum on indictment`                             IS A MAYBE `Maximum term`
    `maximum on summary conviction`                     IS A MAYBE `Maximum term`
    `last day to lay an information`                    IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 1-3, 3C, 3ZA, 24, 24B, 28
@export default The position under the Immigration Act 1971 (UK) for one person: whether they have the right of abode and whether they require leave to enter; if they applied to vary limited leave, whether it is extended by s 3C on the day in question; and for an offence under s 24 or 24B, the maximum imprisonment on indictment and summary conviction and the last day to lay an information on the s 28 extended time limits. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS AN `Immigration case`  @desc The person's status, any leave extension facts and the day in question, and any offence
GIVETH AN `Immigration position`
`the immigration position for` c MEANS
    `Immigration position` WITH
        `right of abode`                                IS `has the right of abode` (c's `the person`)
        `requires leave to enter`                       IS `requires leave to enter` (c's `the person`)
        `leave extended by s 3C on the day`             IS
            CONSIDER c's `a leave extension`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the leave is extended by s 3C under` f `on` (c's `the day in question`))
        `maximum on indictment`                         IS
            CONSIDER c's `an offence`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the maximum on indictment for` o)
        `maximum on summary conviction`                 IS
            CONSIDER c's `an offence`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the maximum on summary conviction for` o)
        `last day to lay an information`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `an offence`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN `the last day to lay an information for` o
